 id:"LP3-01", title:"Planning a Presentation on Recycling", category:"Environment", band:6, mock:null, part:3,
 voices:{H:"us_f", R:"gb_m2"},
 lines:[
 ["R","So, Hana, the recycling presentation is on the twelfth. Shall we finally sort out what we're going to say?"],
 ["H","Yes, definitely. I've been thinking about the focus. At first I wanted to cover recycling in general, you know, plastics, glass, paper, everything. But there's just far too much for fifteen minutes."],
 ["R","Agreed. I was going to suggest we stick to plastics, since that's what everyone talks about."],
 ["H","Well, that's the problem, isn't it? Everybody does plastics. I'd rather look at food waste. Hardly anyone in our year has chosen it, and the figures for the campus are really striking."],
 ["R","Hmm. I suppose that would make us stand out. OK, food waste it is."],
 ["H","Good. Now, the audience. Doctor Okafor said the session is open to first-years as well, not just our seminar group."],
 ["R","Right, so we can't assume they know the technical terms. We should explain what composting actually is quite early on."],
 ["H","Makes sense. And how about opening with a video? There's a good two-minute one made by the local council."],
 ["R","I'm not sure. Videos always seem to go wrong with the projector in that room. Last time ours had no sound at all. Why don't we begin by putting a question to the audience instead? Something like, how much food do you think the canteen throws away every week?"],
 ["H","Oh, I like that. It gets people involved straight away, and it's a nice way into the numbers."],
 ["R","Speaking of numbers, the canteen manager gave me the figures last week. It's around four hundred kilos a week, apparently."],
 ["H","Four hundred? I thought it was more like three hundred."],
 ["R","That was last year's figure. It's gone up since they extended the opening hours in the evenings."],
 ["H","Wow. So how should we show that? A pie chart?"],
 ["R","A pie chart won't really show change over time. I'd go for a line graph, going back five years."],
 ["H","Actually, I'd say a simple bar chart, one bar for each year. Line graphs can look a bit cluttered on a slide, and people at the back won't be able to read them."],
 ["R","Fair enough. A bar chart, then. Right, so who's doing what?"],
 ["H","Well, I'm happy to design the slides. I've got the software at home, and I quite enjoy that kind of thing."],
 ["R","Great. Then I'll get in touch with the canteen manager again. There are a couple of numbers I need to double-check with her."],
 ["H","Oh, and someone needs to interview a student from the environment society about their compost project. I could do it, but I'm away this weekend."],
 ["R","Leave that with me. I know their president, so it'll be easy to arrange."],
 ["H","Thanks. What about the handout? I think we should write that together, half each, and then swap and check each other's part."],
 ["R","OK, that sounds fair. And the list of references at the end?"],
 ["H","I'll do that. I'm used to the referencing style from my history module, so it won't take me long."],
 ["R","Brilliant. And obviously we need to rehearse together, ideally twice. How about Thursday and Monday, in one of the library group rooms?"],
 ["H","Perfect. I'll book a room for both days."],
 ["R","Then the final thing is the questions at the end. I'd rather you took those. You're much better at thinking on your feet than I am."],
 ["H","Hmm, I'm not sure about that. Couldn't we split them? If it's about the data, you answer, and if it's about the interview... oh, wait, you're doing the interview."],
 ["R","Exactly. So it all comes back to me unless you agree."],
 ["H","Fine. I'll handle the questions, but you have to jump in if I get stuck."],
 ["R","Deal. I'll send you the canteen figures tonight so you can start on the bar chart."]
 ],
